this is only a CE gitlabs over HTTP
very simple and direct

ssh doesnt work:
Port 22 isn't exposed, so git clone git@... won't work — only HTTP cloning.

no htts:
Traffic over port 8080 is plain HTTP

No SMTP/email:
No mail server configured, so password resets, notifications, and CI alerts won't send emails.

No resource limits:
No CPU/memory limits set. GitLab CE is heavy (~4GB RAM at idle) and can starve the host.

No backup:
Data lives in Docker named volumes with no automated backup strategy.

NO runner:
There's no GitLab Runner container, so CI/CD pipelines have nowhere to execute.

Single node, no HA
Everything (Postgres, Redis, Gitaly, Puma, Sidekiq) runs inside one container. No redundancy.

For a home lab it's fine, but the two most immediately impactful missing pieces are usually SSH port exposure and a GitLab Runner for CI/CD.